hansraj316/loop-creator  0.1.0 -> 0.2.0
change_type: instructions   changelog: 0.2.0: refined triggering description (hand-reviewed, not benchmarked — the automated trigger-scoring harness could not detect skill triggering via 'claude -p' in this environment). Sharpens the trigger to a self-running loop with a judged outcome + real stop condition, and explicitly excludes near-misses: literal loop code, plain vercel.json/GitHub-Actions cron, and the Vercel Workflow product. Skill body unchanged.

### SKILL.md  [instructions]
-   Use this to design and build an agentic LOOP — a self-running system that
-   triggers itself, does work, checks the result against a hard gate, records
-   state, and decides what happens next — rather than a one-off prompt. Trigger
-   this whenever the user says "build me a loop", "set up a loop", "make this run
-   on a schedule", "automate X to run every morning/hour/day", "have an agent keep
-   doing X", "run this unattended", "design a recurring agent/routine", "triage X
-   automatically", or describes any recurring/background task they want to keep
-   working after they close the laptop — even if they don't say the word "loop".
-   Also use when turning an existing manual chore (CI triage, PR review, digest
-   emails, dependency bumps, doc refresh) into something that runs without them.
-   Produces a complete, safe, well-defined loop: a trigger, a state file, a
-   procedure skill, hard stop conditions, a command allowlist, and a supervised
-   rollout — not just a prompt.
+   Use this when the user wants you to BUILD a self-running agent loop — take a
+   recurring chore and turn it into something that fires on its own (a schedule or
+   event), does the work, checks the result against an OBJECTIVE pass/fail gate,
+   records state to disk, and repeats until a real stopping condition — so it keeps
+   working after they stop prompting. The tell is a judged outcome plus a trigger,
+   not just a timer. Trigger on: "build me a loop / set up a loop", "automate this
+   whole flow so it just runs every few hours", "turn my weekly/standup chore into
+   something self-running", "keep fixing/triaging X and re-running until it's green,
+   then stop", "check Y for me unattended", "every morning read yesterday's failures
+   and write them up", "add the checker half that grades what my bot produces", or
+   any background/recurring task they want to hand off. Covers CI triage, PR
+   review/merge-checking, digests, lint/build loops, dependency bumps, doc refresh.
+   Delivers the whole system — trigger, state file, procedure skill, hard-stop gate,
+   command allowlist, supervised rollout. Skip for: one-off tasks done now, writing
+   literal loop code (a Python while/for-loop or an infinite-render bug), and plain
+   scheduling with no work-or-gate (a vercel.json cron, a GitHub Actions YAML).